File: lib/OCP/Secrets.pm:370-385, 486-503, 546-564

karr #86 added `_assert_key_matches_project`, but it is only called on the WRITE paths (`decrypt_age_key_with_password` at line 300). The READ paths (`read_all_secrets` 370-385, `read_kubeconfig` 486-503, `decrypt_file` 546-564) slurp `secrets_file` / `keys_file` / `kubeconfig_file` and hand the local `.ocp/age.key` straight to `File::SOPS->decrypt`. When the local key cannot open the committed files the user sees File::SOPS's opaque "could not decrypt data key with any of the provided identities" instead of the named-recipients error that karr #86 promised.

Each read helper must call `_assert_key_matches_project` before slurping the encrypted file, exactly as the write path does.

Repro:
1. Commit secrets.yaml encrypted with age recipient age1A...
2. Drop an unrelated age1B... key into .ocp/age.key
3. Run `ocp status`
Observed: opaque SOPS error. Expected: error naming both recipients (the karr #86 contract).
